This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The overarching project ("vertumnus", in `~/code/vertumnus`) is a **static, printable web poster** of in-season farmer's-market produce, week-granularity (52 weeks), distinguishing "available" (weight 25) vs "peak" (weight 100 = best & cheapest), with swappable region data files (first region: SF Bay Area). This continuation session covered, in order:
   - Set up a way for the assistant to visually verify the poster (Playwright attempted, failed under bun/node; pivoted to Bun.WebView headless screenshots).
   - Code-quality refactors: rename `dev-region`→`testRegion`; validate testRegion in the schema test; move peak-midpoint SORT to zod **validation** (throw ZodError on unsorted, NOT a transform); merge `calendar.ts` into `season.ts`; move `MIN_WEEK`/`MAX_WEEK` into `season.ts`; make `Level` an as-const object enum; extract per-produce `color` into the region DATA (validated hex, `z.enum(Level)`, remove `Availability`); replace `buildPoster`/`PosterModel` with the colocated `Ribbons` component; rename `samples`→`slices` and `hi`/`lo`→`top`/`bottom`.
   - Label placement: edge-aware horizontal clamping (Meyer Lemon fix), vertical centering via ±window averaging, adaptive font sizing (shrink for long name / narrow peak), and word-wrapping labels across lines.
   - Reintroduce `Poster` (framed container). Iterated frame color to a faded sage `#cbd7be`, straight outer corners (paper) + rounded inner chart card, title centered, dark-green title.
   - URL-as-state: a `queryParams` hook (`useSyncExternalStore`, no context) with zod parsing + defaults; `hideBanner` flag; then `w`/`h`/`unit` paper params.
   - `Banner` component: intro banner open by default, dismissible to a bottom-right floating icon. Later added Framer Motion `layoutId` morph, lucide icons, hover states, cursor:pointer fix, intro copy + Wikipedia link, split into `BannerContent`(layout)+`Intro`(fragment).
   - `PaperSizeSelector`: collapsible; presets (landscape) + Custom width/height inputs + in/cm toggle; state as `w`/`h`/`unit` URL params; presets derived from value match; convert on unit toggle.
   - **Envelope-math hoist (most recent major task)**: make the WHOLE poster adopt the paper's aspect ratio (so it prints on one page and screenshots correctly), with a fixed border; chart fills the interior; ribbons fill via derived scale.
   - Update `docs/session.jsonl` transcript.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Stack: Bun native `bun build` (NOT Astro/Vite) + React 19 SPA (client-only), TypeScript 7 (native tsc), Tailwind v4 (via bun-plugin-tailwind), oxlint + oxlint-tailwindcss + oxfmt, zod v4, d3-shape, motion (Framer Motion) 12.42.2, lucide-react 1.25.0.
   - `Bun.WebView` headless screenshots: `new Bun.WebView({width,height})`, `await view.navigate(url)` (waits for load; NOT constructor `url`), `await view.screenshot()`, `view.close()`. Used to "see" the poster. `qlmanage -t` also rasterizes SVGs.
   - Playwright is a Node tool that CANNOT run under bun (throws `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME`/`bun:` protocol errors even under `node cli.js` with Node 26.5 + @playwright/test 1.61.1). Removed it.
   - Dev server MUST be started from the project root (else `bunfig.toml`/tailwind plugin not loaded → unstyled render). Dev server goes stale on NEW/renamed files (500 "Could not resolve") → restart required (edits HMR fine).
   - zod v4: `z.number()` already rejects NaN/Infinity by default (`.finite()` deprecated/redundant); `.catch(v).default(v)` pattern for URL params; `.transform` vs `.refine` (user wanted refine to reject unsorted, not transform-sort); `z.enum(UNITS as const)`.
   - Tailwind v4 Preflight has NO button `cursor: pointer` (removed in v4 — controversial "silent removal"); restored via `@layer base { button:not(:disabled),[role='button']{cursor:pointer} }`. `@import 'tailwindcss'` includes Preflight (reset/normalize) inlined in index.css's base layer — no separate normalize needed.
   - Streamgraph geometry: constant-total-height stacking with slack distributed as equal inter-ribbon gaps (bottom anchored); derived `WEIGHT_SCALE` = `(content - (n-1)*ROW_GAP)/maxWeight` fills the box.
   - ResizeObserver + `useLayoutEffect` + synchronous `getBoundingClientRect` measure (avoids initial blank-frame flash; the observer's first callback is async relative to paint, so a synchronous measure is required).
   - CSS `aspect-ratio: {w}/{h}` makes the whole poster the paper shape; SVG viewBox = measured px box → 1 unit = 1 real px (crisp text, no distortion from transform-scale).
   - Framer Motion: `layoutId` shared morph; `whileHover` on the SAME property as a timed reveal caused a regression (fixed by using CSS `hover:brightness-90` filter instead).

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **src/components/Ribbons.tsx** (most recent, heavily restructured): Split into self-sizing `Ribbons` + fixed-size `Streamgraph`. The outer measures via ResizeObserver; the inner derives scale from the measured box.
     ```tsx
     import { area, curveBasis } from 'd3-shape';
     import { useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
     import type { Produce, Region } from '@/data/types';
     import { LEVEL_WEIGHT, Level, MONTHS, peakMidpoint, spanWidth, WEEKS_PER_YEAR, weeklyWeights } from '@/lib/season';
     const PAD_X=12; const PAD_TOP=40; const PAD_BOTTOM=16; const ROW_GAP=6;
     const MAX_FONT=12; const MIN_FONT=8; const CHAR_W_RATIO=0.6; const LABEL_WINDOW=3; const LINE_H=1.15;
     interface Slice { x:number; top:number; bottom:number }
     interface Label { x:number; y:number; font:number; lines:string[] }
     interface Ribbon { name:string; color:string; path:string; label:Label }
     interface Geometry { cellW:number; gridW:number; peakHeight:number; weekToX:(week:number)=>number }
     const areaGen = area<Slice>().x(d=>d.x).y0(d=>d.bottom).y1(d=>d.top).curve(curveBasis);
     export function Ribbons({ region }: { region: Region }) {
       const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
       const [size, setSize] = useState({ width: 0, height: 0 });
       useLayoutEffect(() => {
         const el = ref.current;
         if (!el) return;
         const measure = () => { const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect(); setSize({ width: rect.width, height: rect.height }); };
         measure(); // synchronous first measure so the initial paint is filled, not empty
         const observer = new ResizeObserver(measure);
         observer.observe(el);
         return () => observer.disconnect();
       }, []);
       return (<div ref={ref} className="h-full w-full">{size.width>0 && size.height>0 && (<Streamgraph region={region} width={size.width} height={size.height} />)}</div>);
     }
     function Streamgraph({ region, width, height }: { region: Region; width: number; height: number }) {
       const { ribbons, months } = buildStreamgraph(region.items, width, height);
       return (<svg className="block h-full w-full font-sans" viewBox={`0 0 ${width} ${height}`} role="img" aria-label={`In-season produce for ${region.name}`}> ...months...ribbons(path + <RibbonLabel {...r.label} />)... </svg>);
     }
     ```
     `buildStreamgraph(items,width,height)`: `gridW=width-PAD_X*2`; `weekToX=(week)=>PAD_X+((week-1)/WEEKS_PER_YEAR)*gridW`; `weights=items.map(i=>weeklyWeights(i.spans))`; `sumPerWeek`; `maxWeight=Math.max(0,...sumPerWeek)`; `content=height-PAD_TOP-PAD_BOTTOM`; `scale=maxWeight>0?Math.max(0,content-Math.max(0,n-1)*ROW_GAP)/maxWeight:0`; geometry `{cellW:gridW/WEEKS_PER_YEAR, gridW, peakHeight:LEVEL_WEIGHT[Level.Peak]*scale, weekToX}`; `maxSum=maxWeight*scale`; `gapAt=(wk)=>n>1?ROW_GAP+(maxSum-(sumPerWeek[wk]??0)*scale)/(n-1):0`; stacking loop with `bottom=top+(w[wk]??0)*scale`; `fullSlices` extends to weekToX(53); returns `{ribbons, months}`. Helpers: `placeLabel(item,slices,geo)` (uses `fitLabel(item.name, peakWeeks*geo.cellW, geo.peakHeight)`, clamp to `[PAD_X+half, PAD_X+geo.gridW-half]`, `averageCenter`), `averageCenter`, `fitLabel(name,peakPx,peakHeight)`, `wrapWords`, `clamp`.

   - **src/components/Poster.tsx** (final): reads paper params; sage frame at paper aspect ratio; chart fills remaining height.
     ```tsx
     import { Ribbons } from '@/components/Ribbons';
     import type { Region } from '@/data/types';
     import { useQueryParams } from '@/lib/queryParams';
     export function Poster({ region }: { region: Region }) {
       const { w, h } = useQueryParams();
       return (
         <article className="mx-auto flex max-w-5xl flex-col bg-[#cbd7be] p-8 shadow-lg" style={{ aspectRatio: `${w} / ${h}` }}>
           <header className="text-center"><h1 className="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-green-900">{region.name}</h1></header>
           <div className="mt-6 min-h-0 flex-1 rounded-xl bg-white p-3"><Ribbons region={region} /></div>
           {/* TODO: footer — source citations as fine print + a link back to vertumnus */}
         </article>
       );
